<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ankober</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ankober is a town in the highlands of North Shewa in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, on the edge of the escarpment above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> lowlands. From the 18th century it was the capital of the rulers of Shewa, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahle-selassie">Sahle Selassie</a> in the 19th century it received British and French diplomatic missions. Its importance faded after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> moved his court south, eventually founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>.</p></div>
